---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Therapist Website Design Process | Brighter Sites"
  description="A straightforward website design process for therapists and counseling practices."
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>

      <h1>A clear process from first conversation to launch.</h1>

      <p class="page-lead">
        You do not need to know anything about web design. We guide the project,
        explain the decisions that matter, and keep the process understandable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="process-grid">
        <div class="process-step">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Discover</h3>
          <p>
            We learn about your practice, clinicians, services, ideal clients,
            location, goals, and what you want the website to communicate.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Plan</h3>
          <p>
            We decide which pages are needed and organize the information so
            visitors can move through the site naturally.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Design</h3>
          <p>
            We establish the visual direction—colors, typography, imagery,
            spacing, navigation, and page layouts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Build</h3>
          <p>
            The approved direction becomes a responsive website with working
            navigation, mobile layouts, metadata, analytics, and the technical
            pieces needed for launch.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>Refine</h3>
          <p>
            You review the actual website and we adjust content, layout, and
            presentation where needed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <span>06</span>
          <h3>Launch</h3>
          <p>
            We connect the domain, complete final checks, and put the finished
            website online.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container process-support-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What we need from you</p>
        <h2>You provide the practice knowledge. We handle the web work.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Your practice information</h3>
          <p>
            Who you serve, what services you offer, clinician information,
            location details, and how clients should contact you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Your preferences</h3>
          <p>
            Colors, styles, examples you like, imagery preferences, and anything
            you definitely do—or do not—want your site to feel like.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Your feedback</h3>
          <p>
            You review the work as it develops so the finished site accurately
            represents your practice.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">No technical background required</p>

        <h2>You should not have to become a web designer to get a good website.</h2>

        <p>
          Our job is to handle the implementation while giving you clear,
          understandable choices about the parts that affect your practice.
        </p>

        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Start a project</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
